        "content": "<p>Is there an existing definition of Euclidean relation (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_relation\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_relation</a>)? I couldn't find it mathlib. We're working on modal logic in CSLib and it's an important concept there. I'm using a temporary <code>abbrev</code> for now.</p>",
        "id": 591700272,
        "sender_full_name": "Fabrizio Montesi",
        "timestamp": 1777445619
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The current abbrev, for reference:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RightEuclidean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591700631,
        "sender_full_name": "Fabrizio Montesi",
        "timestamp": 1777445762
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think this is in Mathlib. Extracting a PR to <code>Cslib.Foundations.Data.Relation</code> for now seems reasonable.</p>",
        "id": 591800243,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1777470151
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is not a controversial concept to define but for the records there is also:<a href=\"https://github.com/FormalizedFormalLogic/Foundation/blob/master/Foundation/Vorspiel/Rel/Euclidean.lean\">https://github.com/FormalizedFormalLogic/Foundation/blob/master/Foundation/Vorspiel/Rel/Euclidean.lean</a></p>",
        "id": 591811397,
        "sender_full_name": "Matteo Cipollina",
        "timestamp": 1777472453
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nice, I'll link to that FFL module in our docs if we add any similar lemmas in a follow-up PR.</p>",
        "id": 591815570,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1777473314
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks, and agreed.</p>",
        "id": 591823559,
        "sender_full_name": "Fabrizio Montesi",
        "timestamp": 1777475108
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think, we should extract the relation library for our repo (FFL) (below <code>Vorspiel/Rel</code>), because, euclidean (5) and isolated (Ver), seriality (D), convergent (.2), etc. are important relation properties for modal logic.</p>",
        "id": 594783940,
        "sender_full_name": "SnO2WMaN",
        "timestamp": 1778661501
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(i don't know other area of application Euclidean relation, except modal logic.)</p>",
        "id": 594784387,
        "sender_full_name": "SnO2WMaN",
        "timestamp": 1778661618
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd certainly welcome a PR to CSLib so we don't duplicate any of your work. In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/cslib/pull/557\">cslib#557</a> I added a few additional lemmas about Euclidean relations and now have some more in a branch. I also noticed that Mathlib has <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Relator.LeftTotal#doc\">docs#Relator.LeftTotal</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Relator.RightTotal#doc\">docs#Relator.RightTotal</a> which is the same as serial and its dual.</p>",
        "id": 594789612,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1778662957
    }
]